## Decision Matrix

| Scenario | Strategy | Implementation |
|----------|----------|----------------|
| Static navigation/header | Regular component | Place in page.tsx outside Suspense |
| Slow-changing config | `'use cache'` | Use with `cacheLife('hours')` |
| User dashboards/tables | Client `useQuery` | Wrap in Suspense boundary |
| Interactive filters | `useQuery` + `useTransition` | Prevents Suspense fallback |
| Real-time notifications | `useQuery` with short `staleTime` | Auto-refetch on focus |
| Mutations (CRUD) | `useMutation` | With `invalidateQueries` |

---

## Summary

**Architecture:**
- PPR enabled via `cacheComponents: true`
- Static shell renders instantly from CDN
- Suspense boundaries for each dynamic section
- Client-side `useQuery` for fresh, interactive data
- Optional `'use cache'` for slow-changing server data

**Benefits:**
- ✅ Fast initial page load (static shell)
- ✅ Fresh data on every visit
- ✅ Simple, maintainable code
- ✅ Great UX (streaming, optimistic updates)
- ✅ Type-safe end-to-end
- ✅ Flexible caching strategies